summary:
  The declared notification is set to autoDelete, which kills every later caller.

history:
  Released and unnoticed for a long time: with autoDelete true, KNotification
  frees the object after the first notification of a session. Everything that
  tried to notify afterwards — stream errors, the recording finished message,
  the alarm fallback tone — silently did nothing. notify() is the only door,
  so one wrong flag muted the whole widget.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
    autoDelete: false

replace:
    autoDelete: true

expect:
  The dev.sh lint rule that greps declared notifications for autoDelete: true
  (scripts/dev.sh, written for this very incident) — that is what kills this
  mutant today. A behavioural test that fires two notifications in one session
  and asserts the second still lands does NOT exist yet; if the lint rule is
  ever dropped, this mutant survives and this line is the diagnosis.
